Here's the structured goal model based on the mission description:

### Goal Model

| Goal ID | Goal Title | Text | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation |
|--------|------------|------|--------------------|-----------|----------|
| G1     | Complete Resource Collection and Delivery | Ensure resources are collected from storage and delivered to the specified location. | # | Perform | - |
| G2     | Execute Collection Phase | Collect required resources from storage locations. | ; | Perform | G1 |
| G3     | Execute Delivery Phase | Deliver collected resources to the specified location. | FALLBACK(G3.1, G3.2) | Perform | G1 |
| G2.1   | Navigate to Storage Location | Move to the designated storage area. | - | Perform | G2 |
| G2.2   | Request Resources | Send a message to the storage with resource specifications. | - | Query | G2 |
| G2.3   | Wait for Retrieval | Wait until resources are retrieved from storage. | - | Perform | G2 |
| G2.4   | Recharge Battery | Return to the recharging station when battery is low. | - | Perform | G2 |
| G2.5   | Assign Mission to Another Robot | Transfer mission to another robot when battery is low. | - | Perform | G2 |
| G3.1   | Deliver All Resources | Transport all resources to the specified location. | - | Perform | G3 |
| G3.2   | Handle Battery Low in Delivery | Return resources to a checkpoint and assign remaining task. | - | Perform | G3 |

### Task Model

| Task ID | Task Title | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|---------|------------|------|----------|----------|------------------|---------------|
| AT1     | Navigate to Storage | Move to the storage area. | AND | Storage Area | 1 | Single robot navigates. |
| AT2     | Request Resources | Send resource request message. | AND | Storage | 1 | Single robot communicates. |
| AT3     | Wait for Retrieval | Wait until resources are ready. | AND | Storage | 1 | Single robot waits. |
| AT4     | Recharge Battery | Go to recharge station. | AND | Recharge Station | 1 | Single robot recharges. |
| AT5     | Assign Mission | Transfer mission to another robot. | AND | Recharge Station | 1 | Single robot assigns mission. |
| AT6     | Deliver Resources | Transport resources to destination. | AND | Delivery Location | [1, n] | Multiple robots may deliver. |
| AT7     | Return to Checkpoint | Bring resources back to checkpoint. | AND | Checkpoint | 1 | Single robot returns. |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3 [AND]**: Both collection and delivery are required for the mission to succeed.
- **G2 -> G2.1, G2.2, G2.3 [AND]**: Sequential execution for collection.
- **G2 -> G2.4, G2.5 [FALLBACK]**: If battery is low during collection, recharge and assign another robot.
- **G3 -> G3.1, G3.2 [FALLBACK]**: Deliver all resources or handle low battery during delivery.

This model ensures that the mission is decomposed into manageable goals and tasks, with appropriate handling of battery constraints and parallel execution for efficiency.
